  clock: 4  # daf5
  nonce: daf5  # daf5
  message: "DONE — PR #224, dev 25ef8937c5. 21978 passed, 100% coverage, mypy ratchet clean at 672.\n\nWHERE THE GATE WENT, and why not where the item's own red test predicted. New\n_catalogue_key_for_edge, called from the index site that populates callee_names. NOT in\n_qualified_callee: gating key CONSTRUCTION would break\ntest_in_repo_callee_key_has_no_file_extension, which pins the INV-rozaj fix. The key SHAPE was\nnever the defect — handing a first-party key to a catalogue that describes stdlib and third-party\nsurfaces was. Candidate (b)/(c) from the filing, using the predicate ADR-0037 ruling 4 names.\n\nPREDICATE: only an edge whose is_resolved is falsey may be catalogued. Read from the FIELD, never\nfrom the dst string's :unresolved suffix — WI-pubiv's boundary-id remap rewrites that suffix to\n:external_symbol on the final graph, so a string check would read every unresolved edge as\nresolved and bypass the gate entirely. Pinned by its own test.\n\nMEASURED EFFECT: ZERO, and the zero is readable because the instrument has a positive control\n(meas/zumud_exposure.py, persisted). Across 55,779 taint call edges on caddy + pretix, 2,668\nmatched a shipped qualified key BEFORE the gate and 2,668 AFTER — nothing refused. The control is\na synthetic resolved edge whose key is deliberately a real shipped key (Array.prototype.filter);\nit IS refused, so the zero is absence rather than a broken predicate. The filing had sized this\nonly on a hypergumbo self-survey (0 collisions / 72,822 edges, 42 of 69 shipped keys shadowable in\nprinciple) and said explicitly it had never been measured on the cohort. It now has been, on two\nof the seven, with the same answer.\n\nDIRECTION, argued not assumed. A summary that says \"terminates\" lets the section 3a walk CLOSE a\nbranch, and a false close REMOVES a real finding. Refusing to catalogue can only produce FEWER\nterminations, hence more unknowns and more surviving violations. The .get(\"is_resolved\", True)\ndefault carries the same direction: an edge with no resolution verdict — an older artifact, a\nhand-edited map — is treated as first-party and is not catalogued (L54 default-deny; the\nPERMITTING case is enumerated, namely \"the callee is known to be external\").\n\nTWO CLAIMS IN THIS ITEM'S OWN SHIPPED RED TEST CORRECTED IN PLACE.\n  1. It predicted \"if a guard lands, it should FAIL and be rewritten to assert the guard\". It did\n     NOT fail, and should not have, for the reason above. Its docstring now records that the\n     prediction about itself was wrong and points at TestCatalogueKeyProvenanceGate.\n  2. Its urgency argument rested on \"section 3a is confirm-only and NOTHING ACTS ON False\". The\n     first half still holds — adjudicated = (walk is True) collapses False and None. The second\n     half has been FALSE since PR #214: the same-function sanitizer path runs a SECOND walk whose\n     False earns `sanitized`, and a sanitized flow is dropped from a claim's violation set. A\n     False does act today. That is why this landed now rather than being deferred to WI-kabif's\n     removal authority.\n\nFIVE TESTS, and the shape is deliberate: the defect; a POSITIVE CONTROL that an unresolved\nexternal edge IS still catalogued (without it the gate could refuse everything and pass); the\ndefault-deny case; the ADR-0037 field-not-suffix case; and a WIRING test that captures the actual\ncallees_at index propagate_taint_ddg hands the walk, because a predicate nobody calls is not a\nfix. The wiring test asserts the walk actually ran before asserting anything about the index.\n\nUNBLOCKS WI-kabif-dahad-kufuz-vodoz-misaj-batut-honab-nizib (the isbefore was real: this is the\ninsurance that had to exist before removal authority is granted)."  # daf5
